# Providers — one key, many models (OpenRouter)

## What this file is

The **LLM layer**. A provider decides how you reach a model and what it costs.
A **router** (OpenRouter) lets you reach many models with one API key.

## Generic (vendor-neutral)

```jsonc
{
  "provider": "<provider-name>",
  "model": "<vendor>/<model-id>",
  "apiKey": "$PROVIDER_API_KEY"
}
```

Pick a provider by: capability, cost, latency, privacy, reliability.

## opencode-specific — `providers.openrouter.jsonc` (copy this)

```jsonc
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",

  "provider": {
    "openrouter": {
      // opencode resolves OpenRouter through its AI-SDK provider.
      // Confirm the current package name in the docs.
      "npm": "@openrouter/ai-sdk-provider",
      "options": {
        "apiKey": "{env:OPENROUTER_API_KEY}",
        // Optional attribution headers some routers use:
        "headers": {
          "HTTP-Referer": "https://ghw.mlh.com",
          "X-Title": "AI Coding Assistant Best Practices"
        }
      },
      // You can pin which models appear in the picker:
      "models": {
        "<vendor>/<model-id>": {},
        "<vendor>/<small-model-id>": {}
      }
    }
  },

  // Then reference them with the provider prefix:
  "model": "openrouter/<vendor>/<model-id>",
  "small_model": "openrouter/<vendor>/<small-model-id>"
}
```

## Set the key once (never in the repo)

```bash
# ~/.zshrc or your shell profile
export OPENROUTER_API_KEY="sk-or-..."
```

> Model IDs and the provider package name change frequently. Check the
> OpenRouter model list and your tool's docs before copying verbatim.
